You offer the Amulet of Yendor to Ptah
An invisible choir sings, and you are bathed in radiance...
The voice of Ptah booms out: "Congratulations, mortal!"
"In return for thy service, I grant thee the gift of Immortality!"
You ascend to the status of Demigoddess...

Rianne the wizard was the latest in a long line of wizards bearing
similar names - Rianne, Rianna, Rosaline, Rosa etc., for those of you
Hearse users who may have found bones files of previous unfortunate
incarnations.

While it appears odd for an Elvish wizard to be lawful, this was in
fact a split second decision made to save my "life". I visited the
left altar guarded by Pestilence first, since on my previous attempt
Famine had killed me rather nastily. It was the wrong one. So I headed
toward the central altar, guarded by Death. In the process I adopted a
number of pets which subsequently died. Charm monster was very useful
for making the priests peaceful, which cut down on the amount of
fighting I had to do. The central altar was also the wrong one. While
I did have a number of amulets of life saving in store, Death's max
hitpoints attacks were seriously damaging (I had 415 Hp when I entered
the Astral Plane), and I was fairly confident that those amulets would
not save me.

As you can see from the screen-shot, I was cornered by both Death and
Pestilence. I had planned badly and not taken enough offensive wands
with me, (although I was burdened stupidly) and the Amulet was
draining my power so that I could not hit either of those Riders with
offensive spells, and the kept regenerating next to me. It seemed that
as soon as I drank a potion and healed up, both Death and Pestilence
would whack me down again. At one point I was down to about 180 Max
HP. I didn't think I would make it to the right altar alive, so to cut
my losses, in desperation I wished for a helm of opposite alignment
and offered the amulet to Ptah. Ptah was obviously pleased with me,
and accepted my alleigence, and granted me the status of Demigoddess!
:)

This game was extremely lucky in terms of finding useful items. In
addition to the castle wand of wishing I found two others, one at
(1:1) and the other at (0:1). I also received a wish from a magic
lamp, so there was an insane amount of wishing going on. Luckily,
since this was my first ascension, I really didn't care about
conducts. Maybe next time. Both of the other wands were found in a
bones pile of my previous character who had been killed by the Wizard
of Yendor on Juiblex's Level. Thanks also to Chris who was killed by a
baluchitherium, whose inventory yielded some interesting items. I
can't remember what, exactly, but it was cool at the time.

This game was also completed using the New Toys set of levels. There
didn't appear to be any special level near level 4, but Minetown
turned out to be the one with a large river running through the middle
of it, with the MineEnd being a mazelike gehennom sort of experience.
The VoTD appeared to be a series of interlinked caves. I personally
think that this set of levels adds some more interest and variation to
the game, which was enjoyable.

Learning the polymorph spell was invaluable, since I managed to
polypile literally hundreds of items to get scrolls of genocide,
attack spellbooks and potions of full and extra healing.

Gehennom was easy this time with a wizard, since magic mapping, good
attack spells, and the ability to teleport really helped. Asmodeus and
Baalzebub were paid off, and went away. Much to my relief I didn't
meet Geryon, Dispater or most importantly Demogorgon in this game. I
was also extremely lucky that the "mysterious force" only pulled me
back about five times. I did die once on the plane of Air
unfortunately - those elementals were simply too tough for me.

I haven't set any records for speed or conduct, or performed any
Stupid Ascension Tricks, but it was great fun, and I'm glad that I
finally succeeded!

